{
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "id": "20596_kougai",
  "headword": "{口外|こうがい}",
  "reading": "こうがい",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "disclosing; revealing (a secret)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "disclosing; revealing; divulging",
      "explanation": "The act of telling others something that should be kept secret or confidential. Almost always used in negative constructions meaning 'do not reveal.'"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20596_kougai_ex1",
      "japanese": "{口外|こうがい}しないでください。",
      "english": "Please don't tell anyone.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20596_kougai_ex2",
      "japanese": "この{件|けん}は{絶対|ぜったい}に{口外|こうがい}してはならない。",
      "english": "You must never reveal this matter to anyone.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20596_kougai_ex3",
      "japanese": "{社内|しゃない}の{機密情報|きみつじょうほう}を{口外|こうがい}した{社員|しゃいん}が{処分|しょぶん}を{受|う}けた。",
      "english": "An employee who disclosed confidential company information was disciplined.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {口|こう} (mouth) + {外|がい} (outside) — literally \"putting outside one's mouth,\" i.e., speaking aloud what should remain unspoken. Almost exclusively used in prohibitive or negative contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {口外|こうがい}しない (not reveal)\n- {口外|こうがい}してはならない (must not disclose)\n- {口外|こうがい}{無用|むよう} (do not disclose; confidential)\n- {口外|こうがい}{禁止|きんし} (disclosure prohibited)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {漏|も}らす — to leak (information), to let slip (more colloquial)\n- {暴露|ばくろ} — exposure, revelation (often of scandals or wrongdoing)\n- {吐露|とろ} — confession, revealing one's feelings (more personal and emotional)",
